---
---

<section class="fc-faq" id="faq">
  <div class="fc-faq-inner">
    <div class="fc-faq-head">
      <div class="fc-eyebrow" style="justify-content: center;">Questions</div>
      <h2 class="fc-h2" style="margin: var(--sp-4) auto 0; max-width: 20ch;">
        Before you arrive.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="fc-faq-list" data-faq-list>
      <details class="fc-faq-item" open>
        <summary class="fc-faq-summary">
          What times and dates are the sessions?
          <i class="ph-light ph-plus"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="fc-faq-answer">
          <p>
            All sessions take place live on Zoom over four consecutive
            Sundays in July 2026 — July 5, 12, 19, and 26.
          </p>
          <p>
            The full schedule, rendered in
            <span class="fc-faq-tz" data-fc-faq-tz>your local timezone</span>,
            is <a href="#schedule">at the top of this page</a>. Reference
            times in three common zones:
          </p>
          <div class="fc-faq-times">
            <div data-fc-faq-row data-iso="2026-07-05T18:00:00Z" data-tz="America/Los_Angeles"><span>Pacific · Los Angeles</span>11:00 AM PDT</div>
            <div data-fc-faq-row data-iso="2026-07-05T18:00:00Z" data-tz="America/New_York"><span>Eastern · New York</span>2:00 PM EDT</div>
            <div data-fc-faq-row data-iso="2026-07-05T18:00:00Z" data-tz="Europe/Brussels"><span>Europe · Brussels</span>8:00 PM CEST</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="fc-faq-item">
        <summary class="fc-faq-summary">
          Are there replays?
          <i class="ph-light ph-plus"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="fc-faq-answer">
          <p class="fc-faq-lead-line">
            Yes — every participant receives lifetime access to the replays.
          </p>
          <p>
            Recordings are posted within 24 hours of each live class, and
            they're yours to keep and revisit — no expiry, no extra cost.
            Whether you join every session live, some of them, or none, you
            receive the full course.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="fc-faq-item">
        <summary class="fc-faq-summary">
          Is this course for me?
          <i class="ph-light ph-plus"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="fc-faq-answer">
          <p>
            If you're carrying unresolved pain — toward others or yourself —
            and you're ready to approach it with honesty and care, this course
            will meet you where you are. No prior experience with sounding or
            forgiveness work is required.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="fc-faq-item">
        <summary class="fc-faq-summary">
          Do I need a spiritual or religious background?
          <i class="ph-light ph-plus"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="fc-faq-answer">
          <p>
            No. The course is open to all belief systems. We draw from diverse
            sources — including the Enneagram, ho'oponopono, and A Course in
            Miracles — but no prior knowledge or affiliation is needed.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="fc-faq-item">
        <summary class="fc-faq-summary">
          Is this course about forgiving others or forgiving myself?
          <i class="ph-light ph-plus"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="fc-faq-answer">
          <p>
            Both. And, as the work deepens, a third layer emerges — the
            forgiveness of separation itself. We move through all three, in
            their natural order.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="fc-faq-item">
        <summary class="fc-faq-summary">
          What is Somatic Vocal Healing?
          <i class="ph-light ph-plus"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="fc-faq-answer">
          <p>
            <strong>Somatic Vocal Healing</strong> is a practice founded by
            Jacob Vermeulen. It uses intentional sound-making — not singing,
            not chanting, not breathwork — to access and release what the body
            holds beyond words. In this course, sounding becomes the somatic
            key that allows forgiveness to move from idea to lived experience.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  // Accordion: opening one closes the others, matching the React prototype.
  const items = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLDetailsElement>('[data-faq-list] .fc-faq-item');
  items.forEach((item) => {
    item.addEventListener('toggle', () => {
      if (item.open) {
        items.forEach((other) => {
          if (other !== item) other.open = false;
        });
      }
    });
  });

  // Localize the FAQ reference times into each named timezone and surface
  // the visitor's own timezone label in the surrounding sentence.
  const rows = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-fc-faq-row]');
  rows.forEach((row) => {
    const iso = row.getAttribute('data-iso');
    const tz = row.getAttribute('data-tz');
    if (!iso || !tz) return;
    const d = new Date(iso);
    const timeFmt = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', {
      hour: 'numeric', minute: '2-digit', timeZoneName: 'short', timeZone: tz,
    });
    const label = row.querySelector('span');
    if (label) {
      row.textContent = '';
      row.appendChild(label);
      row.appendChild(document.createTextNode(timeFmt.format(d)));
    }
  });

  const tzLabel = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fc-faq-tz]');
  if (tzLabel) {
    const tz = Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone;
    if (tz) tzLabel.textContent = `your local timezone (${tz.replace(/_/g, ' ')})`;
  }
</script>
